A||||12||Bill Shenefelt||Decent shocks and struts||||1||
Z||000000||Bill Shenefelt||12-23-2001||08:39 PM||||I just picked up a 4 cyl 86 that needs both shocks and struts.  In my 6 cyl I had gone to sears- I think they were gabrial, but not sure.  Fiero store has monroe, and two brands of air shocks.  I think and I probably dont want to go the full route for an expensive set, but if necessary.....<BR>What is decent and where is the best place to go for them, local Automotive supply?  What brand??<BR>Bill Shenefelt||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||12-23-2001||08:55 PM||||I'm pretty happy with Gabriels on my '85 SE.  I use the car for daily driving and occasional mountain flogging.  If you want performance shocks, KYB probably gives the best bang for the buck; however, they're about twice the price of Gabriel.  I bought my shocks and struts at AutoZone.<P><BR><I>Edited for grammar</I><BR><p>[This message has been edited by MrPBody (edited 12-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-24-2001||10:57 AM||||I used Gabriel when I recently did mine. <A HREF="http://www.gabriel.com" TARGET=_blank>www.gabriel.com</A>  available at Pep Boys, others.<P>Pro Ryder Gas Shocks with VST<BR>Gas Ryder Struts with VST<P>there's an article in my cave about this.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||12-24-2001||05:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MrPBody:<BR><B>If you want performance shocks, KYB probably gives the best bang for the buck; however, they're about twice the price of Gabriel.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Unless you paid less than $75 for both struts and both shocks KYB's are not twice as much!  <P>KYB struts run $52 apiece and the shocks are $16 apiece ($136 total.....about $150 w/shipping from tirerack.com).  They are, in my opinion, the best shock/strut for the money.  <P>If you can afford KONI's then that's the route to go, but KYB's are far superior to Monroe, Gabriel, et al. (again, my opinion).  The fact that they are the same price, or in some cases cheaper, makes them that much better. <P>If you do decide on something other than KYB I would highly suggest <B>NOT</B> getting the Monroes......I used these once and they were pure junk.  The Gabriels would be next in line for me if KYB's were suddenly unavailable. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||12-24-2001||08:07 PM||||mrfiero --<P>I priced both KYB and Gabriel from local sources -- NOPI and Autozone respectively.  Although KYBs weren't exactly twice the price of Gabriels, they were close to it.  Believe me, if I had found KYBs for the prices you cite, I would have bought them!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by MrPBody (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||12-24-2001||08:11 PM||||If you buy KYB's buy them from <A HREF="http://www.tirerack.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tirerack.com</A>   <P>They generally have the lowest prices. <P>What were the stores quoting you for the KYB's?  How about the Gabriels?<P>Just curious.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||12-24-2001||08:59 PM||||I bought KYB's and I like them a lot. Monroe's are "cheap" replacements, Gabriel's are OK.<BR>I bought my KYB's last year for $45.00 for the pair of front shocks and $90.00 for the pair of rear struts. (These were the prices including shipping for the pair) I bought them on sale from the Fiero Store. The regular prices are on the high side. The Tire Rack has a good price. If you search on-line you may find some slightly cheaper but Tire Rack has great customer service and fast shipping.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||12-24-2001||10:37 PM||||I got a set of KYB's from Tire Rack for about $170, including shipping for all four.  (Gas-A-Just front, GR-2 rear)  I really like them.  Great stuff, unless you wanna pop for Koni's.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfiero||12-24-2001||10:45 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>I got a set of KYB's from Tire Rack for about $170, including shipping for all four.  (Gas-A-Just front, GR-2 rear)  I really like them.  Great stuff, unless you wanna pop for Koni's.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I guess I should have specified......the GR-2 front shocks are $16 and the stiffer Gas-A-Just are $29.......still a great price, considering "stock" replacements run about $20-$25 apiece.<P>Speaking of sale prices (that's a good price from the Fiero Store BTW!), I remember buying KYB's from CarParts.Com way back when they fist opened up.  They had these 1/3 off coupons on top of their super low prices......I bought a set of KYB's for just <B>under</B> $100!  Those were the days!  They don't even carry KYB's anymore (plus their prices are MUCH higher now to boot).<P>At any rate.....I am a big proponent of KYB's, so I always recommend them to everyone (I even got my mom to get them for her grocery getter Beretta!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||MrPBody||12-24-2001||11:04 PM||||mrfiero --<P>Working from my unreliable memory, I'm pretty sure that NOPI had KYB Gas-A-Just front shocks for about $32 each.  I don't remember the price of KYB struts, although I think they were priced in scale with front shocks.  This was more than a year ago.  NOPI's online catalog no longer lists Fiero shocks, so I can't verify current pricing tonight.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||WampusCat||12-24-2001||11:15 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012476.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/012476.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||12-25-2001||12:53 PM||||At Pep Boys, I paid (caryout 9/29/01)<BR>19.99 per shock, List according to PB- 49.41 Pro Ryder gas<BR>34.99 per strut, List according to PB- 93.78 Gas Ryder<BR>I don't believe that was a sale either.<P>They are both top end products and feature Gabriel's VST valve that functions during both bump and rebound modes.<P>I got cam bolts, Monroe AK-30, from Advance Auto for about $8 per side. ( <A HREF="http://www.PartsAmerica.com" TARGET=_blank>www.PartsAmerica.com</A>  ) They were the only parts store that didn't give me a raft of crap trying to find them. (Way cheaper than NAPA.) I also got my spring compressor from them. That was about $25. <P>I've got the sport suspension already... I didn't want or really need the increased stiffness you'd likely get with a monotube shock like I think the KYBs are.<P>VST is explained at Gabriels web site.<P>I've always had my doubts about the varios velocity sensitive valve systems... Now you coudn't give me shocks w/o it. VST works as well or better than billed. VST has also made a serious dent in whatever bump steer problems I've had.<P>There's a diagonal RR Xing on my way to work... That thing would have the car bouncing any which way with the old struts and shocks. Now I just roll right over it w/o hardly noticing. (Old ones were factory struts, which were crap when installed, and Monore gas shocks.)<P>If you're going to race a car heavily then you might want KYB or Koni, but for daily driving and an occasional race, the Gabriels are going to be hard to beat at that kind of pricing.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||wcapman||12-25-2001||03:48 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.eshocks.com" TARGET=_blank>www.eshocks.com</A>  has the Konis for 168 per strut.  Anyone know a cheaper source?||||reg||1
